      en: "The Nizhny Pyanj river port is situated on the Panj River at the border between Tajikistan and Afghanistan, serving as a critical logistics hub for cross-border trade. Its significance grew immensely with the opening of the U.S.-funded bridge in 2007, which replaced the ferry service and revolutionized the movement of goods between Central and South Asia. The port and the adjacent customs terminal handle a large portion of Tajik imports, including fuel, food products, and construction materials. Simultaneously, it acts as the primary gateway for exporting agricultural goods to Afghanistan and further onto Pakistan. The facility is equipped with modern storage warehouses and loading cranes designed to manage the increasing volume of transit traffic. As part of international transport corridors, Nizhny Pyanj plays a key role in the economic integration of the region and the strengthening of trade ties.",
